The Mercedes-Benz Vito Dualiner Comfort is a variant of the W447 generation Vito Crew Van, focusing on enhanced passenger comfort and features. The W447 generation has been in production since 2014 and received updates in 2019/2020 and a significant facelift in 2024. The "Comfort" designation typically implies a higher trim level than the base models, incorporating more car-like amenities.

Based on the search results, the most recent Vito (2024 facelift) offers "Select" and "Pro" trims, with "Comfort" features often being part of the "Progressive" or "Select" trims in earlier W447 models or standard on the updated models. The Dualiner (Mixto) body style is available in the current lineup. Engine options for the diesel Vito are now primarily a 2.0-litre unit with various power outputs (136hp, 163hp, 190hp - 114, 116, 119 CDI). Rear-wheel drive is standard, with a 9-speed automatic transmission common on higher power outputs.

The 2024 facelift brought significant interior updates, including a 10.25-inch touchscreen with MBUX, Apple CarPlay, and Android Auto, and improved materials. Safety features are strong, with the latest model earning a Platinum rating from Euro NCAP. The ride is generally considered comfortable and car-like for a van. Cargo space is substantial for a crew van, though less than a panel van.

